Worthy councillor,

The council sat this morning touching the pensions of the religious. Opinions=
 were divided, but the King's will carried the day.

Heads will roll if the venison is late a third time.

Your faithful servant,
Lord Chancellor Thomas Audley

--
This dispatch is intended for the named recipient and may contain matters tou=
ching the Crown. If delivered in error, return it to the Master of the Posts =
and destroy all copies.

